UR_NOTES_EN={
 'time-plans':'Use bajay (بجے) with clock times. Kal (کل) can mean yesterday or tomorrow; the verb and context clarify the meaning. Confirm the day as well as the time.',
 'shopping':'Chahiye (چاہیے) is used for a singular item; chahiyein (چاہئیں) for plural items. Distinguish a question about price from one about quantity.',
 'directions':'Use respectful instruction forms jaen (جائیں), muren (مڑیں) and ruken (رکیں). Saath (ساتھ) means beside, while saamne (سامنے) means in front/opposite in context.',
 'past-weekend':'Urdu past forms depend on gender and sentence structure: main mila/mili (میں ملا/ملی). Hum ne khana khaya (ہم نے کھانا کھایا) uses ne with this completed transitive action. The Bilal example uses masculine forms.',
 'appointments':'Kya hum ... kar saktay hain? (کیا ہم ... کر سکتے ہیں؟) politely proposes a change. A female speaker can replace chahta hoon with chahti hoon, and bhej doon ga with bhej doon gi.',
 'advice':'Aap ... kar saktay hain gives an option; aap ko ... karna chahiye gives advice; ... karna zaroori hai expresses necessity. Explain the reason and avoid presenting every suggestion as an obligation.',
 'compare-options':'Use zyada/kam (زیادہ/کم) with an adjective to compare. Kyun ke (کیونکہ) introduces a reason. State the criterion rather than saying one choice is best for everyone.',
 'email-request':'A clear request gives context, a specific action and a deadline. Jummay tak (جمعے تک) means by Friday. Likh raha hoon/likh rahi hoon varies with the speaker.',
 'evidence-summary':'Mumkin hai (ممکن ہے) and ba-zahir (بظاہر) qualify a claim. Nateeja behtar hua reports an observation; mashq hi sabab thi makes a stronger causal claim.',
 'contingencies':'Agar ... to (اگر ... تو) links a condition to its consequence. Warna (ورنہ) introduces the alternative. Use jab tak ... na (جب تک ... نہ) carefully in context.',
 'respectful-disagreement':'First acknowledge the shared goal, then use kya ...? to question an assumption politely. Describe the concern and a test instead of attacking a person.',
 'resolve-complaint':'Acknowledge the impact without inventing facts. Ittila dene ka waqt (اطلاع دینے کا وقت) is an update deadline, not a guaranteed resolution. The support-agent example uses feminine forms.',
 'interview':'Distinguish main (میں, I) from hum (ہم, we). State an actual responsibility and observable result. Verb agreement depends on the sentence, not simply on changing every ending for the speaker.',
 'meeting':'Use tajweez ki (تجویز کی), ittefaq hua (اتفاق ہوا) and faisla hua (فیصلہ ہوا) accurately. Include the action, zimmedar shakhs (ذمہ دار شخص) and aakhri waqt (آخری وقت).',
 'negotiation':'Use agar (اگر) for a condition and identify what changes in return. Explicitly confirm kaam ki had (کام کی حد), timing and acceptance; a suggestion is not yet an agreed promise.',
 'presentation':'Structure a recommendation as problem, proposal, evidence/uncertainty, risk and decision. Ghair yaqeeni (غیر یقینی) states uncertainty; give a verification step rather than inventing a number.'}
